name: Julia (quaternion)
family: Julia
desc: Quaternion Julia set for q² + c, rendered as a 3-D surface by inverse iteration (q ← ±√(q − c) in the k = 0 slice). The j-term c_j drives the depth — set it to 0 for the classic flat 2-D Julia set.
ref: A. Norton, "Generation and display of geometric fractals in 3-D", SIGGRAPH 1982
tags: julia, fractal, 3d
warmup: 30
ic: 0.5 0.5 0.1
camera: 30 20 0 1

param c_re = -0.2 [-2, 2] "Real (scalar) part of c."
param c_im = 0.6 [-2, 2] "i part of c — shapes the classic 2-D dendrites."
param c_j = 0.3 [-1, 1] "j part of c — drives the 3-D depth; 0 collapses to the flat Julia set."

tw = x - c_re
tx = y - c_im
ty = z - c_j
vm = sqrt(tx*tx + ty*ty)
mag = sqrt(tw*tw + tx*tx + ty*ty)
r = sqrt(mag)
theta = 0.5*atan2(vm, tw) + select(rand() < 0.5, 0, pi)
sw = r*cos(theta)
svm = r*sin(theta)
k = select(vm > 1e-9, svm/max(vm, 1e-9), 0)
x' = sw
y' = select(vm > 1e-9, k*tx, svm)
z' = select(vm > 1e-9, k*ty, 0)
